1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,276
Welcome to Daily Brief.

2
00:00:02,226 --> 00:00:06,142
It's Tuesday, November 24th, 2026.

3
00:00:06,142 --> 00:00:08,809
Three stories in about three minutes.

4
00:00:08,809 --> 00:00:12,071
First, the biggest corporate story of the year.

5
00:00:12,071 --> 00:00:19,916
Nvidia's board has unanimously voted to restore Jensen Huang as chief executive, and the market's reaction was extraordinary.

6
00:00:19,916 --> 00:00:27,190
The stock rose thirty one percent in a single session, adding close to a trillion dollars in market value in one day.

7
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:34,214
According to US media reports, President Trump personally called Nvidia's board to encourage Huang's return.

8
00:00:34,214 --> 00:00:37,380
The company has not commented on that account.

9
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:45,797
Whatever the full story is, the message from investors was unambiguous: they want the founder back at the helm of the world's most valuable chipmaker.

10
00:00:45,797 --> 00:00:48,714
Second, a tragedy in Indonesia.

11
00:00:48,714 --> 00:00:55,773
A fire at a candy factory in the country has killed at least twenty four people, with around thirty still unaccounted for.

12
00:00:55,773 --> 00:01:00,000
Search teams paused overnight and were due to resume on Monday.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,916
Local officials say the cause is still under investigation.

14
00:01:03,916 --> 00:01:11,119
Factory safety has been a recurring concern in the region, where rapid industrial growth has often outpaced enforcement.

15
00:01:11,119 --> 00:01:14,952
Third, more money moving into artificial intelligence.

16
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:21,630
Amazon has agreed to pay seven and a half billion dollars for technology from Decart, an AI startup.

17
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:29,309
Separately, Cisco and OpenAI announced a joint project called Shirudo, aimed at making agentic AI systems safer.

18
00:01:29,309 --> 00:01:39,857
The two deals point in the same direction: the industry is now spending serious money not just on building smarter models, but on securing them and buying up the niche players who know how.

19
00:01:39,857 --> 00:01:42,083
That's your briefing for today.

20
00:01:42,083 --> 00:01:44,940
The full transcript is in the show notes.

21
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,154
I'll be back tomorrow morning.

